<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE gsdoc PUBLIC "-//GNUstep//DTD gsdoc 1.0.3//EN"
 "http://www.gnustep.org/gsdoc-1_0_3.xml">
<gsdoc base="Tests">
  <head>
    <title>Testing OnTheWing - Your Digital Nature Journal</title>
    <author name="Graham Lee">
      <email address="grahamlee@acm.org"/>
    </author>
    <version>1.0</version>
  </head>

  <body>
    <front>
      <contents/>
    </front>

    <chapter>
      <label id="testing"/>
      <heading>Testing OnTheWing</heading>
      <p>Ensure you have the prerequisites set up, as described in <ref id="development-prereqs">Install Prerequisites</ref>.
      To run the tests in your computer's operating system instead of in a container environment, you also need to install GNUstep's <uref url="https://github.com/gnustep/tools-xctest">XCTest</uref>.</p>

      <section>
        <heading>Run Unit Tests</heading>
        <p>Use this command to run the tests in your computer's operating system:</p>
        <example>
        % make check
        </example>
        <p>Use this command to run the tests in the container environment:</p>
        <example>
        % make podman-check
        </example>
      </section>

      <section>
        <heading>Run End-to-End Tests</heading>
        <p>Use this command to run the tests in a browser in your computer's operating system, with the app running in minikube:</p>
        <example>
        % make test-e2e
        </example>
        <p>Use this command to run the tests in a headless browser in the minikube cluster alongside the app:</p>
        <example>
        % make test-e2e-cluster
        </example>
      </section>
    </chapter>

    <back>
      <index type="title" scope="project" style="normal"/>
    </back>
  </body>
</gsdoc>
